ctr: a system folder per game, over the BIOS the CIA carries

The system folder is the manifest's system_dir, the game's own
<data_dir>/system on the SD card. When the CIA carries BIOS files
(romfs:/bios, packed by the injector from the user's bios/<core>/ folder)
RetroArch and the core see that folder through "sys:/", a small device
that lays the SD card folder over the CIA's: a file is read from the SD
card when it is there (a BIOS added or replaced later, without
reinstalling) and from the CIA otherwise; whatever a core writes (MAME's
settings, nvram, hiscores) goes to the SD card. Nothing is copied.

The folder is exported as LIBRETRO_SYSTEM_DIRECTORY, which RetroArch
applies after the config file: it wins over a system folder saved in the
game's retroarch.cfg by an older build of the CIA.

Applies on top of 0005, to RetroArch v1.22.2 (RETROARCH_REF in versions.env).

